<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AUTOQUIP YEAR INCOME UP 38 PCT, HOLDS DIV.</title>
<headline>AUTOQUIP YEAR INCOME UP 38 PCT, HOLDS DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 35.5	  vs 25.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.5	   vs same </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.89	  vs 2.82</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.29	  vs 4.02</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.16	  vs 0.92</p>
<p>    Turnover		  94.45	 vs 79.35</p>
<p>Full name: Autoquip Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Autoquip, which is a wholesaler and retailer of car</p>
<p>parts, said its dividend is payable to holders of preference</p>
<p>shares. The group said, as in the past, no dividend has been</p>
<p>declared on ordinary shares though it would be considered once</p>
<p>the preference shares have been redeemed.</p>
<p>The firm said slower economic growth, a spiralling crime</p>
<p>wave and a more competitive market would make trading difficult</p>
<p>in the coming year. But the group added it anticipated a real</p>
<p>increase in earnings growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
